  "verified_mechanisms": [
    "Rust resolves pre-order sibling order, parent indices, depth and inherited visibility from UI IDs and folder flags. No URLs, titles, profile objects or native View pointers cross the tree ABI.",
    "Rust owns collapse state under separate workspace/item keys. Hidden descendants remain in the plan and native hierarchy, preserving nested collapse state during parent expand/collapse.",
    "The tree regression collapses a child and parent, renames the hidden child, reconstructs rows, switches workspaces, then verifies both collapse states and reveals the grandchild in order.",
    "The existing new-folder dialog expands a collapsed parent before creating its child. The browser regression verifies the new child is drawn at the expected indentation.",
    "Rust unit tests cover sibling ordering, retained hidden descendants, workspace isolation including delimiter-containing IDs, state reset, duplicate/empty IDs, orphans, unreachable cycles, leaf parents and the 64-level bound.",
    "The native swipe preview consumes the same plan. Native painting and spacing remain adapters; a pinned pair consumed by a hidden folder is not added again among ordinary preview tabs.",
    "The 300-pin warm-sidebar tests pass without additional native list builds, context-menu visits or pin-visibility bookkeeping during warm workspace switching.",
    "Existing row input, split/pinned-pair geometry, scroll, scene text, paint suppression, workspace swipe, persistence/rollback, palette and settings regressions pass in the Metal backend."
  ],
  "manual_observations": [
    "The signed isolated app displayed the Unicode split pair and the indented folder/pin tree.",
    "Collapsing the Project folder removed its Documentation pin from the visible accessibility tree and moved the tab list up.",
    "Cmd+Alt+2 switched to the separate private profile; Cmd+Alt+1 returned with Project still collapsed and the split pair intact. Screenshot and accessibility state agreed.",
    "Expanding Project restored Documentation. The demo retains its original 24 work tabs, split pair and expanded folder; the prototype was closed.",
    "The normal app and browser profile were not used."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Native View containers, event/focus/accessibility and menu adapters remain. The application still places pinned split pairs into the hierarchy, persists browser state and owns folder editing forms.",
    "The C++ plan/state implementation remains the default Views baseline; the opt-in Metal path uses the Rust implementation.",
    "The immediate command-rejection path restores prior collapse state in source. The new dialog regression exercises successful creation; existing folder regressions exercise asynchronous failed writes.",
    "Large-list test timings are not a controlled CPU/GPU/presentation comparison. This report uses their cache-invariant assertions and does not claim an end-to-end speedup.",
    "Full VoiceOver/IME, non-macOS integration and the remaining outer controls/forms still require verification and migration.",
    "No third-party crate, library or binary framework was added."
  ]
